###Setting up a proportion

Corresponding sides of similar triangles are proportional, so we can set up and solve a proportion:

$\dfrac{WY}{WK}=\dfrac{KW}{ZW}$

Side $\overline{WY}$ is equal to $\overline{WZ}+\blueE{\overline{YZ}}$ and we need to find the length of $\blueE{\overline{YZ}}$.

We picked side $\overline{WK}$ because it corresponds to side ${\overline{WY}}$.

Then we picked another pair of corresponding sides where we already knew the measurements.

$\begin{array}{rcl}
&\triangle KWY
\\
{\text{hypotenuse}}
&\overbrace{\underbrace{\!\!\!\!\!\left\{ 
\dfrac{WZ+\blueE{YZ}}{WK}=\dfrac{KW}{ZW}
\right\}\!\!\!\!\!}}
&{\text{long} \atop \text{leg}}
\\
&\triangle ZWK
\end{array}$
